From 9b76d23bcc39e10d99172db36aa1f70b43f33264 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: portability-fix <portability-fix@local>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 05:12:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: make pip install and pytest collection work on
 non-Windows platforms

requirements.txt:
- MetaTrader5==5.0.5735 now carries the PEP 508 marker '; sys_platform == "win32"'.
  The package publishes win_amd64 wheels only (cp36..cp314), so a plain
  'pip install -r requirements.txt' previously aborted on Linux/macOS.
  Windows installs are byte-for-byte unchanged.
- Declare pydantic==2.13.5 explicitly (directly imported by src/api/schemas.py;
  previously only a transitive pin of fastapi).

tests (9 files): the module-level _mt5_available()/_live_available() probes that
feed @pytest.mark.skipif called MetaTrader5.initialize()/connect() at import time.
Where the real package is absent, tests/conftest.py's import-only stub refuses the
call, which turned into 9 collection errors and aborted every pytest run on
non-Windows. Each probe now returns False instead of propagating, so live-gated
tests SKIP honestly (the behavior the stub's own error message prescribes) and the
offline tests in those files run. Windows behavior is unchanged.

tests/conftest.py: add TIMEFRAME_W1 (32769) to the stub constants table --
src/mt5/market_data.py reads mt5.TIMEFRAME_W1 at import time, matching the stub's
documented policy for import-time-read constants; fixes
test_topdown_market_data.py::test_w1_registered_in_mt5_acquisition_mapping.

Verified on Linux/Python 3.13: fresh venv install exits 0 (MT5 skipped via marker,
pip check clean); pytest collects 3,745 tests with zero collection errors;
3,619 passed / 48 skipped / 37 failed, where all 37 failures are pre-existing
categories already recorded in the 2026-09-21 readiness audit (dataset fingerprint
mismatch, hardcoded D:\\ paths, stale frozen-scope baselines, contract drift,
unmarked runtime MT5 tests) -- none introduced by this change.
